Relevant columns (how they will be used)  
• `event_date`            : filter rows to December 2020 (`'20201201'–'20201231'`).  
• `event_name`            : identify session rows (`event_name = 'session_start'`).  
• `event_params`          : – key = `ga_session_id`   → numeric session id  
                           – key = `medium`           → traffic‑medium string  
                           – key = `source`           → traffic‑source string  
• `traffic_source.medium` : already parsed medium (if present).  
• `traffic_source.source` : already parsed source (if present).  
• `user_pseudo_id`        : user identifier – together with `ga_session_id` forms one session.  

Typical channel‑grouping CASE logic (simplified subset)  
CASE  
  WHEN source = '(direct)'            AND medium IN ('(not set)','(none)')                         THEN 'Direct'  
  WHEN REGEXP_CONTAINS(medium, r'push|mobile|notification')                                         THEN 'Mobile Push Notifications'  
  WHEN medium = 'referral'                                                                           THEN 'Referral'  
  WHEN REGEXP_CONTAINS(medium , r'display|banner|cpm|interstitial|expandable')                       THEN 'Display'  
  WHEN REGEXP_CONTAINS(medium , r'email|e-mail|e_mail|e mail') OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(source , r'email') THEN 'Email'  
  WHEN REGEXP_CONTAINS(medium , r'ppc|cpc|paid')  AND REGEXP_CONTAINS(source , r'(bing|google|yahoo|baidu)') THEN 'Paid Search'  
  … ELSE 'Unassigned' END AS channel

